            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "special+holonomy#Leung02"}> Leung 02
              )
          %h3#rozanskywitten_weight_systems Rozansky-Witten weight systems
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyperkähler manifold
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+weight+system"} Rozansky-Witten weight system
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in certain
            = succeed "-groups." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+cohomology"} Dolbeault cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            there are induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+weight+system"} Rozansky-Witten weight system
            with values in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#compact_hyperkhler_manifolds Compact hyperkähler manifolds
          %p
            The only known examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{[n+1]}
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            either
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
                (in which case the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
                is really the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{T}^4)^{[n]} \to \mathbb{T}^4
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Beauville83"}> Beauville 83
            ) and two exceptional examples (
            %a{:href => "#OGrady99"}> O’Grady 99
            ,
            %a{:href => "#OGrady03"} O’Grady 03
            ), see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sawon04"} Sawon 04, Sec. 5.3
          %h3#coulomb_and_higgsbranches_of___sym
            Coulomb- and Higgs-branches of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} =4
            SYM
          %p
            Both the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coulomb+branch"} Coulomb branch
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+branch"} Higgs branch
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theories"} D=3 N=4 super Yang-Mills theories
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} hyperkähler manifolds
            (
            %a{:href => "D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#SeibergWitten96"}> Seiberg-Witten 96
            , see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "D=3+N=4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#dBHOO96"} dBHOO 96
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            (
            %a{:href => "D=3+N=4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#Intriligator99"}> Intriligator 99
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"}> Kähler manifold
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong hyper-Kähler manifold
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} quaternionic Kähler manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} compact hyperkähler manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} ADE singularity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+theory"} Rozansky-Witten theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperkähler_manifold"} Hyperkähler manifold
          %h3#compact_hyperkhler_manifolds_2 Compact hyperkähler manifolds
          %ul
            %li#Beauville83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variétés Kähleriennes dont la premiere classe de Chern est nulle
              %p
                Diff. Geom. 18 (1983), 755–782 (
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214438181"}> euclid.jdg/1214438181
                )
            %li#OGrady99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kieran+O%E2%80%99Grady"}> Kieran O’Grady
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Desingularized moduli spaces of sheaves on a K3
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9708009"} arXiv:alg-geom/9708009
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9805099"} arXiv:math/9805099
            %li#OGrady03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kieran+O%E2%80%99Grady"}> Kieran O’Grady
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A new six dimensional irreducible symplectic variety
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0010187"} arXiv:math/0010187
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Huybrechts"}> Daniel Huybrechts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Compact Hyperkähler Manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calabi-Yau Manifolds and Related Geometries
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-19004-9_3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-19004-9_3
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9705025"}> arXiv:alg-geom/9705025
                )
          %h3#rozanskywitten_invariants Rozansky-Witten invariants
          %p
            With an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+theory"} Rozansky-Witten theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"}> ground field
            \-valued
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+weight+systems"} Rozansky-Witten weight systems
          %ul
            %li#RobertsWillerton06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Roberts"}> Justin Roberts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Willerton"} Simon Willerton
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Rozansky-Witten weight systems
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0602653"} arXiv:math/0602653
            %li#Sawon04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Sawon"}> Justin Sawon
                , Section 5.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rozansky-Witten invariants of hyperkähler manifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404360"} arXiv:math/0404360
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p
            The example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coulomb+branches"} Coulomb branches
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=3 N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            originates with
          %ul
            %li#SeibergWitten96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"}> Nathan Seiberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gauge Dynamics And Compactification To Three Dimensions
              %em The mathematical beauty of physics: A memorial volume for Claude Itzykson
              Proceedings, Conference, Saclay, France, June 5-7, 1996 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9607163"}> arXiv:hep-th/9607163
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/420925"} spire:420925
